            "question": "Your destructor deletes a raw pointer. <em>What else</em> must you write?"
          }
        },
        {
          "type": "graph",
          "say": "Here is a string class that owns a raw buffer and frees it in its destructor. Copy it, and the compiler's copy constructor copies the pointer, not the buffer. Now two objects share one allocation. When the copy is destroyed, the buffer is freed. When the original is destroyed, it frees the same memory again: a double free, which is undefined behavior.",
          "props": {
            "title": "A shallow copy, <em>a double free</em>",
            "nodes": [
              {
                "id": "s1",
                "label": "s1  (data_)",
                "x": 220,
                "y": 340,
                "w": 240,
                "h": 64
